# PostHog. Both are read at build time by components/analytics/PostHogInit.tsx
# and inlined into the client bundle, so neither is a secret: the project key is
# write-only and is meant to ship in the browser. Set them in the Vercel project
# (Settings > Environment Variables) and copy this file to .env.local for dev.
#
# Leave NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY unset to disable PostHog entirely, which is the
# sane default for local work so dev traffic stays out of the project.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# US cloud is the default when unset. Use https://eu.i.posthog.com for EU cloud.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# GA4 is not here on purpose: the measurement ID is public, fixed, and the same
# everywhere, so it lives in site.config.ts with the other integration values.
